From 5d2fd2bc33fde4e5c0c461b6c549cf329d7e0082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:56:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Thompson: graupel at or below R1 goes to vapour instead
 of being deleted

WRF's copy of Thompson balances graupel mass and number separately from
rain and, where the graupel left after the source and sink terms is at or
below R1, overwrites its tendency to delete it (qgten = -qg1d/dt). The M5
commit sent leftover rain to vapour but left this branch, which the CCPP
copy does not have. Trace rain freezing (prg_rfz ~1e-15) in supercooled
layers feeds it. Add the leftover graupel to vapour with lsub, as for rain.

Found by a column red team (double-precision harness, 1000 plausible
columns): the WRF port's water residual reached 2.7e-10 kg/m2 (relative
2.6e-11, 50 columns above 1e-12), against 5.7e-14 for the CCPP copy; the
deleted graupel's fusion heat stayed in the temperature. Compiles
(gfortran syntax check); not yet rerun in the harness or WRF.

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
---
 phys/module_mp_thompson.F | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/phys/module_mp_thompson.F b/phys/module_mp_thompson.F
index 86999ae5..a624e71c 100644
--- a/phys/module_mp_thompson.F
+++ b/phys/module_mp_thompson.F
@@ -3192,6 +3192,9 @@
             endif
 
          else
+           ! graupel left at or below R1 goes to vapour with its latent heat, not deleted
+           qvten(k) = qvten(k) + (qg1d(k) + qgten(k)*dtsave)*odts
+           tten(k) = tten(k) - lsub*ocp(k)*(qg1d(k) + qgten(k)*dtsave)*odts*(1-IFDRY)
            qgten(k) = -qg1d(k)*odts
            ngten(k) = -ng1d(k)*odts
            qbten(k) = -qb1d(k)*odts
